{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Method Overloading.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Method Overloading.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c method overloading c method overloading","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Method Overloading.md","fileName":"C# Method Overloading.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Method Overloading","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C Sharp Object-Oriented Type Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Object-Oriented Type Design","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Method Overloading.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Method Overloading.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c method overloading c method overloading","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Method Overloading.md","fileName":"C# Method Overloading.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Method Overloading","heading":"C# Method Overloading","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Method overloading defines several members with the same name but different parameter signatures. The compiler selects an overload from the number, types, order, and passing modes of the arguments supplied at the call site.\n\nOverloads present one conceptual operation across several input forms. They should preserve related meaning; unrelated behavior hidden under one name makes selection harder to understand. Return type alone cannot distinguish overloads because it is not part of the call's argument signature.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Object-Oriented Type Design","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Method Overloading.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Method Ov